 ops/changelog.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ops/changelog.md b/ops/changelog.md
index d32689f8b2..60ec5a31b8 100644
--- a/ops/changelog.md
+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -9989,3 +9989,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-23: PHASE A6 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY; INTEGRATION + HEADLINE METRIC) -- consolidate whatever RAISED a real metric (A1 graded goal-energy -> live solve-rate/first-win; A2 expansion prior -> deeper live solve; A3 new bank) into the SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG + the refreshed package; re-measure end-to-end on live solve-rate + live_multi_level_solve_rate + action efficiency + offline_to_live_transfer_ratio + live-submittable count (vs 33). If NONE raised a clean control-passed metric (each gated by its positive control + uniform-energy ablation), keep the bare config + honest null. Avoid the .427 solve-rate TAUTOLOGY (a bare==integrated equality is a null, not a fabrication). Keep test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py + arc_orphan_solver_lint green. verifier_is_oracle: false. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: integrated_live_submittable_raised_config_shipped; results/experiment_4645_integration_gate.json
 - 2026-06-23: PHASE B1 (RESERVED INFRA; co-headline metric) -- add a canonical live_multi_level_solve_rate metric helper: the fraction of live attempts that solve >=2 levels (the NEW WALL -- .427 reached first-win 0.59 but multi-level solve-rate is 0.04), reported SIDE-BY-SIDE with reproducible_total_levels, live-submittable count, first-win-rate, live_action_efficiency, and offline_to_live_transfer_ratio. This is the metric that distinguishes "reached the first level-up" from "solved multiple levels live" -- the gap A1/A2 must close. Asserting tests. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: live_multi_level_solve_rate_metric_helper_shipped_tests_green; results/experiment_4646_live_multi_level_solve_rate_metric.json
 - 2026-06-23: PHASE B2 (RESERVED INFRA; adversarial_verify hardening -- the GOAL-ENERGY-WITHOUT-ABLATION guard) -- add a reader-side guard: an ARC artifact claiming an ENERGY-DRIVEN-GENERATION win (graded goal-energy / energy heuristic / energy-as-fitness raised live solve-rate/first-win) MUST report a UNIFORM-ENERGY ABLATION control that did NOT achieve it -- a win backed only by "energy-on beat the baseline" with no uniform/random-energy ablation WARN-fires (it might be the SEARCH, not the energy). Be NARROW: an artifact that HONESTLY reports the ablation (energy beats uniform) does NOT fire; an artifact reporting an energy magnitude as a diagnostic (no win claim) does NOT fire. Reader/guard only; edits adversarial_verify.py, never the conductor. Asserting tests. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: adversarial_verify_hardened_goal_energy_ablation_guard_tests_green.; results/experiment_4647_adversarial_verify_hardening.json
+- 2026-06-23: PHASE C (HARDWARE CONTINUITY; 1 per attached board) -- per-board reachability audit: KV260 (SSH reachability ONLY, never host SD card), GateMate (openFPGALoader USB detect), PolarFire (SSH). Honest blocked_<board>_<reason> if a board is down. Keeps each attached board visible per the Hardware-Task Continuity Discipline without burning a heavy slot during the ARC sprint. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: hardware_continuity_2_of_3_boards_reachable; results/experiment_4648_hardware_continuity.json
